A||N||10||Tina||Coolant overflow problems||||9||
Z||000000||Tina||09-02-2001||10:43 AM||||Oops,...I mean the coolant overflow tank...<P>Already I'am 5 for 5 on these things.<BR>After noticing a couple of drop of antifreeze on my hood, I started investigating a little.<BR>Only to find a hole in my coolant tank.<BR>No problem I thought. Got 2 more here laying around.<BR>.......Broken........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Well of to the junkjard....found 2 more<BR>.......Broken........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Always damaged in same area.<BR>(Upper left corner, the one close to the radiator. Plastic seems to become brittle, and then just break)<BR>Anybody come up with a fix for this yet?<BR>Or could I be that lucky, and a replacement is still available at the dealer?<P>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>BTW One idea I came up with.<BR>I've I were to find one still in good condition, to perhaps coat in some kinda plastic(Simular to the rubber stuff available to coat tool handles) to avoid this problem in the future.<BR>Problem is, you would not be able to see level of coolant in the tank just by looking at it.<BR>And who knows, would that stuff even stick to plastic?<p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 09-02-2001).]||||reg||9
