Z||000009||87GTZ34||09-05-2001||02:52 PM||||Tina, If you don't find a new one, I found one out of an '88 that is good.  The end of the inner mount is cracked but is not a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000010||NEPTUNE||09-07-2001||02:47 PM||||I just repaired a 3 1/2' crack. First remove, clean and DRY the tank.Then melt the ends of the crack with a bic lighter or pencil torch to stop the crack from spreading (don't worry if you leave a small hole). Next find some epoxy plastic repair cement, the kind that looks like a black double barreled syringe, and mix about twice as much as you think you will need. spread it on and around the crack, then cut a peice of cloth and press that into the cement. then spread a little more on top, making sure the cloth is thoroly saturated. i did this a week ago,and it's still holding. BTW, I live in florida and use the ac constantly!  <p>[This message has been edited by NEPTUNE (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||3
